      '2- Definite Article (The): Used when the noun is specific, unique, or known to both speaker and listener. Major Rules for (The): a- Unique things in nature: the sun, the moon, the earth, the sky, the internet. b- Superlative adjectives: the best, the most expensive, the tallest. c- Musical instruments when played/learned: play the piano, listen to the violin. d- Inventions and animal species in general: Alexander Bell invented the telephone. / The cheetah is the fastest animal. e- Oceans, seas, rivers, canals: the Mediterranean, the Pacific, the Nile, the Suez Canal. f- Mountain ranges and groups of islands (plural): the Alps, the Himalayas, the Bahamas. g- Countries with plural names or political titles (Republic, Kingdom, States): the USA, the UK, the UAE, the Arab Republic of Egypt, the Netherlands. h- The + adjective = plural group of people: the rich (= rich people), the poor, the blind.',
