      'Irregular and Tricky Question Tags: 1- I am late, aren\'t I? (NOT amn\'t I!). But negative: I am not late, am I? 2- Let\'s go out, shall we? But: Let us go (permission), will you? 3- Open the door, will you / won\'t you? (Imperative). Don\'t make noise, will you? (Negative imperative). 4- Everyone / Someone / Anyone / Nobody take a PLURAL pronoun (they) in the tag: (Everyone attended the meeting, didn\'t they? / Somebody called, didn\'t they?). 5- Everything / Something / Nothing take a SINGULAR pronoun (it) in the tag: (Nothing happened, did it?). 6- Statements with negative words (never, rarely, seldom, hardly, scarcely, neither, no, few, little) are ALREADY NEGATIVE, so their tag MUST BE POSITIVE: (He rarely eats meat, does he? / She has no friends, does she?).',
