      'The Anatomy of an Academic Essay: An essay is a formal piece of writing consisting of multiple paragraphs exploring a single topic in depth. The standard structure contains at least four to five paragraphs: Introduction, Body Paragraphs (2 to 3), and Conclusion.',
      '1- The Introduction Paragraph (المقدمة): Contains three essential elements in sequence: a- The Hook (الجملة الجاذبة): The opening sentence designed to grab the reader\'s attention and arouse curiosity. Can be a provocative question, an interesting statistic, a shocking fact, or a general thought-provoking quote. b- Background Information (المعلومات التمهيدية): Two or three sentences giving general context and narrowing the topic from general to specific. c- The Thesis Statement (جملة الأطروحة - أهم جملة في المقال كله): The final sentence of the introductory paragraph. It clearly states the main argument, core purpose, and points that will be developed in the body paragraphs. A strong thesis is specific and debatable.',
